# Windows workaround: this repo's path contains "Q&A". cmd.exe (npm's default
# script shell on Windows) treats a bare "&" as a command separator, which
# breaks every npm script that resolves to a node_modules/.bin/*.cmd shim
# (dev, build, lint, start — see docs/07-progress-log.md session 4). Git
# Bash handles the literal "&" in the path correctly, so scripts run through
# it instead. Requires Git for Windows installed at its default location.
script-shell=C:\\Program Files\\Git\\bin\\bash.exe
